---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/seo/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for TextFixer browser-based text utilities."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <article class="container-page max-w-3xl py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: August 27, 2026</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Acceptance</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      By using {SITE_NAME}, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Service description</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      {SITE_NAME} provides browser-based text utilities. Features may change as we ship new tools.
      The service is provided “as is” without warranties of any kind to the fullest extent permitted by law.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Your responsibilities</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-muted">
      <li>Do not use the site for unlawful purposes.</li>
      <li>Review outputs before relying on them for important work.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for text you paste into the tools.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">No professional advice</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      Readability scores, extractions, and formatting helpers are utilities — not legal, medical, or
      professional advice.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, {SITE_NAME} and its operators are not liable for damages
      arising from use of the site or reliance on tool outputs.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      Questions about these terms: <a class="text-accent underline" href="/contact">Contact</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
